'use strict';
/* =============================================================================
   art.js — raster artwork, keyed by NAME.

   V9 designed for this: "every label is a single <text> node at a known anchor,
   so the image swap is a node-for-node replacement with no layout consequences."
   This is that swap — the Root Hub's app tiles wear the real application icons
   instead of a glyph approximating them.

   WHY A REGISTRY AND NOT A DATA URI ON THE BINDING. render.js derives every
   key's SVG id from its content, and SD.image() dedupes by comparing the URI it
   last sent. If a 6 KB base64 payload rode on the binding it would be walked by
   the FNV hash on every one of 36 keys, 15 times a second. A binding carries the
   NAME; only the renderer ever touches the bytes.

   PROVENANCE. Extracted from the installed applications on this machine and
   downscaled to 96px, which is the largest an icon is ever drawn inside the 144
   viewBox:

     ableton    /Applications/Ableton Live 11 Suite.app/Contents/Resources/app.icns
     rekordbox  /Applications/rekordbox 7/rekordbox.app/Contents/Resources/rekordbox.icns
     proq3      /Library/Audio/Plug-Ins/VST3/FabFilter Pro-Q 3.vst3/Contents/Resources/
                Html/FabFilterLogo128.png
     chrome     /Applications/Google Chrome.app/Contents/Resources/app.icns
     vital      /Library/Audio/Plug-Ins/VST3/Vital.vst3/Contents/Resources/Icon.icns

   V45 — "IF IT EXISTS LOCALLY, USE IT; DO NOT INVENT FAKE SVGS" (Adi's rule).
   Applied honestly, which means reporting what is NOT here. Every plug-in bundle
   on this machine was searched for a product mark, and only two more existed:

     found      Chrome (Adi supplied the path), Vital (Icon.icns)
     no mark    Serum2      — no images in the bundle at all
                SPAN        — Resources/ is empty
                s(M)exoscope— the .vst3 is a bare 5 MB FILE, not a bundle
                bx_meter    — only UI parts (meters, buttons), no logo
                INDEQ, dBComp — only UI parts (KNOB, BG, NEEDLE)
                EQ Eight / Compressor / Glue Compressor — Live DRAWS its device
                            graphics; there are no per-device files in the bundle

   Those keys therefore wear text, not a stand-in drawing. Extracting a plugin's
   background plate or knob as though it were a logo would be exactly the "fake
   icon" the rule forbids, just sourced locally.

   Both are the vendors' own application icons, used to label the key that opens
   that application. Re-extract with:
     sips -s format png -Z 96 <path>.icns --out <name>.png
   ============================================================================= */

window.SOS = window.SOS || {};

SOS.Art = {
  ableton: 'data:image/png;base64,',
  rekordbox: 'data:image/png;base64,',
  proq3: 'data:image/png;base64,',
  chrome: 'data:image/png;base64,',
  vital: 'data:image/png;base64,',
};
